// Phase 10 Plan 07 -- QLT-04's declared composition depth 3, REFUSING
// member. Chain of 4 functions (leaf, f2, f1, caller): leaf declares the
// loan's origin (`-> borrow(buffer) Buffer`); f2 and f1 are BOTH middle
// hops, each locally re-borrowing its own parameter and forwarding that
// borrow one level further in -- exactly mirroring
// relay_depth2_refuse.schway's own single middle hop (`relay`), a
// borrow-returning function cannot merely forward a bare received
// parameter (core.origin_understated), it must locally re-borrow at every
// hop that returns one. What is new at depth 3 and unreachable at depth 2:
// the loan survives TWO middle hops (f2's own hop AND f1's own hop) before
// reaching caller -- "a borrow surviving two hops", the interesting cell
// relay_depth2_accept.schway's owned pass-through (D-10-48) cannot exercise
// at all. This is the fixture that satisfies D-10-48's "at least one
// fixture must carry a BORROW through a MIDDLE hop" requirement: BOTH
// middle hops carry it here, twice as many as relay_depth2_refuse.schway's
// single middle hop.
//
// Twin of relay_depth3_accept.schway: same 4-function shape, same loan
// origin (leaf), same middle-hop re-borrow structure at f2 and f1. Where
// the accept twin's own borrow lives and dies within one middle function
// (crossing only 1 hop, the nearest expressible accepting shape given the
// corevalidate defect its own header documents), THIS fixture's declared
// borrow genuinely crosses all 3 hops in the checked core.Program -- it is
// simply never admitted end to end, for the SAME reason
// relay_depth2_refuse.schway is refused: caller's own `take buffer` conflicts
// with the still-live interprocedurally-extended loan `aliased` carries.
// That conflict is what VARIES WHICH HOP CARRIES the interesting action
// between this pair (D-10-48): the accept twin's borrow-and-take sequence
// lives entirely inside f2 (a middle hop); this fixture's conflicting take
// lives in caller (the top of the chain), exactly like the depth-2
// precedent -- generalized one level deeper, not merely restated.
//
// `check.Program` refuses this fixture on its own, before corevalidate is
// ever consulted (session.CheckCommandFile's fixed check-then-peer
// precedence) -- verified empirically: the emitted diagnostic is
// check.interprocedural_loan_liveness, naming F1 (the hop closest to
// caller) via loan_extended_by_call, exactly mirroring
// relay_depth2_refuse.schway's own diagnostic naming `relay`. (Independently,
// corevalidate.Validate would ALSO refuse this fixture, with
// core.callee_not_callable, for the reason relay_depth3_accept.schway's own
// header documents in full -- but check's own refusal fires first and that
// second, independent refusal is never observed on this path, exactly as
// it is never observed on relay_depth2_refuse.schway today.)
//
// Despite the refusal, the underlying checked core.Program is fully
// formed (4 functions, every declared OpCall intact) -- pathoracle's own
// structural analysis is check/corevalidate-verdict-agnostic by design
// (pathoracle.go's own package doc), so
// TestCompositionDepthCorpusReachesDeclaredBound's corpus walk uses this
// fixture's checked core, not the CLI's own refused verdict, to observe
// the declared depth-3 bound genuinely being reached.
//
// Expected, verified empirically via `go run ./cmd/schway --json check`:
// exit non-zero, status "invalid", exactly one diagnostic with code
// check.interprocedural_loan_liveness. QLT-04.

module phase10.relay_depth3_refuse

export {
  fn caller
}

fn leaf(buffer: Buffer) -> borrow(buffer) Buffer {
  let observed = borrow buffer
  observed
}

fn f2(buffer: Buffer) -> borrow(buffer) Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let forwarded = leaf(borrowed)
  forwarded
}

fn f1(buffer: Buffer) -> borrow(buffer) Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let forwarded = f2(borrowed)
  forwarded
}

fn caller(buffer: Buffer) -> borrow(buffer) Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let aliased = f1(borrowed)
  let delivered = take buffer
  aliased
}
